@misc{ask-hook-manifest-sees-package-imports,
  section  = {ask},
  claim    = {check_hook_set --manifest is the vendoring contract for the shared hooks and it tracks only scripts/ siblings, so a hook reaching a substrate.* module is outside its frame by construction. Measured 2026-09-03, four hooks reach the package while the manifest declares no package requirement for any of them, hook_shellcheck.py among them reading substrate.ratchet_flags at :765 while the manifest prints standalone, and the two at the centre of the wrapper-argument repair, hook_cmdparse.py and hook_structural_query.py, are also in that set. A missing sibling is a loud ImportError at adoption time, whereas an under-reported dependency is an adopter who believes the set is complete, so this fails in the silent direction. Widening the walk, declaring the requirement in the output under any wording, or dropping the reference each close it},
